  "scope": "Maintainer harness SDK isolation and Emscripten build concurrency. Twelve unchanged Linux x64 C/Lake FFI registrations across Node, Deno, and Bun; no full-suite claim.",
  "findings": [
    "An inherited LASM_EMSDK setting overrode the captured SDK while preparing the earlier exit-repaired facades. Those exact configurations remain recorded; their full compiler and host modules were frozen, but external C tools used the developer SDK.",
    "A frozen snapshot now takes precedence over the builder environment. New facades select their captured SDK even when the developer setting is deliberately present. The compiler Wasm and host implementation are unchanged.",
    "Emscripten internal cache builds use EMCC_CORES independently of CMake and Binaryen. The guard now sets it to two and the suite environment preserves it. Full links explicitly use one.",
    "Each engine passed the unchanged Lake FFI and reverse-FFI examples, dedicated-thread compilation, and external boxing. All 7267 original source hashes were unchanged before and after each attempt.",
    "All OOM, cap-hit, throttling, and swap counters remain zero. Memory caps were not raised."
